  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Africa Regional (Kenya, Mozambique, Tanzania): Strengthening State Responses to Transnational Organized Crimes in East Africa (EATOC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Regional policymakers develop policy frameworks on transnational organized crimes (TOC). 2) Investigators, prosecutors, and judicial officers in Kenya, Mozambique, and Tanzania increasingly coordinate their work to identify, prevent and respond to TOC.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: East Africa Association of Prosecutors, East Africa Police Chief Cooperation Organization, Southern African Regional Police Chiefs Co-operation Organization. Indirect beneficiaries: East African Community, governments and wider population of Kenya, Mozambique and Tanzania.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to ensure that investigators, prosecutors and judicial officers in Kenya, Mozambique and Tanzania jointly prosecute transnational organized crimes.</narrative>
  </description>
